  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through next Friday)\n\nUpper level ridge continues to be the main weather driver over \nthe weekend with record high temperatures possible through Monday \nafternoon. It is by Monday afternoon that models want to bring a \nvery weak pacific upper trough through northern Nevada. This \ntrough looks only to serve to help push the upper ridge east as it\nwill have very little moisture associated with it, which may be \nenough for a few showers across the Jarbidge mountains Tuesday. \nHowever chances at this point look to be about 10% at most. By \nWednesday the trough will push into the four corners region, which\nwill allow for upper level ridging to build back in over the \nwestern US, and persist through Friday evening. By next Saturday \nmodels are hinting at a pattern change that may bring more active,\nwetter weather back to Nevada in the form of a northern stream \nupper trough. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: \n \nThere is high confidence in the potential near to record, or \nrecord highs through Monday with high pressure in control.\n\nThere is low confidence for the potential for isolated showers \nfor far northern Nevada Monday night into Tuesday as a weak upper \ntrough moves into Nevada.\n\nThere is high confidence in the return of upper ridging Wednesday\nthrough Friday of Next week.",
